    },
    "body": "The first geometric feedback fit changed packed actions but worsened native answer loss. This change gives the bridge offline credit from actual native token distributions for all120 one-lane H4 interventions, with the original occurrence, producer, immutable keys and readouts fixed. Copy, Period and Stop are recomputed together; the existing integer/table serving policy is retained.\n\nBoth zero-update64-case admissions preserve parent behavior and find better local actions at4,412/4,560 lane-target combinations. This admits a prospective paired fit; it does not establish useful learned attention or hard-action descent. The roadmap now requires genuinely new seeded transfer preparation before update1, since the old preparer would reproduce exposed rows.\n\nValidation at executed source3f7cc4a8 on LinuxCPU:3 native tests,3 gradient/credit tests,release build,format/diff/claim checks;146files returned with exactSHA/file-set equality; independent saved-evidence audit4,576,514checks/0discrepancies. No optimizer, GPU, Metal, native reexecution by the reviewer or aggregate-gradient reconstruction is claimed.\n\nReferences #1552, #1512.\n",
